Create a high-contrast print of a butterfly sitting on a wooden branch using the linocut technique. Use sharp carving tools to cut clean, thin lines into the linoleum block to form the wing veins and carved patterns for the wood texture. Roll black printing ink evenly over the top of the block, keeping the carved cuts clean so the white paper shows through to create strong contrast. Use repeating cut marks to build up visual layering and place clear emphasis on the central butterfly against the background.
